// Adaptive Retail Platform - shared database schema (Step 3)
//
// One PostgreSQL 17 database and one Prisma schema for all 21 modules and all
// four business types. Everything below is structure only; no business logic,
// API endpoint or background job is implemented in this step.
//
// Tenant isolation: business-owned rows carry businessId. Branch-scoped rows
// carry businessId + branchId and reference Branch through the composite
// candidate key (businessId, id), so a row can never point at another tenant's
// branch. The same composite pattern is used for other tenant-scoped parents.
//
// Money: Decimal(18, 2) with an explicit 3-letter currency on every monetary
// record. Quantities: Decimal(18, 3). Unit costs: Decimal(18, 4). No floats.
//
// Stock: StockBalance is the single authoritative on-hand/reserved/in-transit
// source per branch + variant. StockMovement is an append-only ledger; batches,
// allocations and valuation snapshots explain it. Negative available stock is
// prohibited by a database CHECK added in migration SQL (see docs/database).
//
// History: sales, receipts, purchase orders, price lists, stock movements and
// audit events are preserved. Cancellation/void/return are separate records or
// status transitions, never destructive deletes. Archived/deactivated rows are
// retained, not removed.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

